# ALL.mask -- line masks for slobol_tests (FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason), read by corpus_suite_harness.py read_mask_sidecar().
lex	^ +[0-9]+  free bytes$	lex.sbl ends by printing COLLECT() * 5, the free bytes of the heap window times five: a figure of the implementation (skill snobol4 section 7, the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13: never faked, masked in both streams). MEASURED 2026-11-15 on SCRIP 8102d126c at the declared sizes: SCRIP prints 842080, sbl -bf 418495; every other line of the report, the statement count included, is graded exactly.
test/host	^host\(\): [^:]+:[^:]+:.+$	CEO-1344 oracle identity, masked by its three-field shape (the coo's ruling of 2026-11-15, skill snobol4 section 7): HOST() with no argument answers the implementation's own host string, x86-64:unix :Macro SPITBOL 15.01 # under sbl -bf and x86-64:linux:SCRIP under SCRIP since 19fd9bd01; SCRIP does not impersonate SPITBOL, and an empty or one-field answer does not match the mask, so it stays red. The second line, host(0), is graded exactly.
